Z||000001||theogre||01-14-2001||12:27 PM||||Unless there are products I haven't seen, Helicoils usually aren't recomended for something as high torque as a head bolt. Talk to an engine machinist about that. Read the helicoil product data very carefully if you buy them off the shelf. There are diferant kinds for diferant applications.<P>Yes it's metric. no I don't know which. take a good bolt with you when you go after a tap.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mark||01-14-2001||01:10 PM||||Ray,<P>The head bolts on my '86 GT are 11 mm x 1.5.<P>I found this tap at NAPA, about $6.00.<P>I used a siphon pump to suck all the coolant out of the coolant passages, then jammed pieces of rags into the coolant passages to prevent debris from going down in the block.  After chasing the head bolt threads, I vacuumed out all debris, then pulled the rags out of the coolant passages.  Made damn sure I got all the rags out!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mark||01-14-2001||01:12 PM||||I guess I should have said the head bolt thread size and pitch is 11 mm x 1.5.||||reg||1
